 20	/// A widget that displays the rendered output of the Ghostty renderer.
 21	///
 22	/// In the past, Ghostty relied on GTK's builtin `GLArea` to display the
 23	/// rendered output within the GTK-based UI, but this had numerous
 24	/// debilitating limitations.
 25	///
 26	/// Its most significant limitation is that GTK's render lifecycle lives
 27	/// **exclusively on the main UI thread**, from initialization to drawing the
 28	/// rendered framebuffers. This is not only inefficient but also error-prone,
 29	/// as we offload our render work to a dedicated render thread which has
 30	/// to be careful not to access the renderer at the same time as the main
 31	/// thread. Initialization is also far more complex as we had to wait for
 32	/// GTK's OpenGL context to initialize, then we can proceed with initializing
 33	/// the renderer and then the core surface. (The GTK surface widget could not
 34	/// assume it always has a valid core surface, which is obviously absurd!)
 35	/// It was a messy, chicken-and-egg relationship that held us back a lot.
 36	///
 37	/// With our custom `RenderSurface`, the renderer instead renders frames,
 38	/// exports them into DMABUFs, then pushes them into a queue that this widget
 39	/// can consume at its own pace on the main thread, whenever GTK calls for it
 40	/// to be snapshotted. This also allowed us to do triple-buffering and should
 41	/// greatly reduce tearing. Initialization is done on the render thread and
 42	/// always completes before the core surface is created. Furthermore, this
 43	/// surface is actually OpenGL-agnostic, since it operates exclusively on
 44	/// DMABUFs which can also be produced by other graphics APIs like Vulkan.
 45	pub const RenderSurface = extern struct {
 46	    const Self = @This();
 47	    parent_instance: Parent,
 48	    pub const Parent = gtk.Widget;
 49	    pub const getGObjectType = gobject.ext.defineClass(Self, .{
 50	        .name = "GhosttyRenderSurface",
 51	        .classInit = &Class.init,
 52	        .parent_class = &Class.parent,
 53	        .private = .{ .Type = Private, .offset = &Private.offset },
 54	    });
 55	
 56	    const C = Common(Self, Private);
 57	
 58	    pub const Private = struct {
 59	        /// The core surface, used to pull presents from the renderer.
 60	        /// Set by the apprt Surface when it realizes the render surface.
 61	        core_surface: ?*CoreSurface = null,
 62	
 63	        /// The GDK Texture currently being displayed.
 64	        texture: ?*gdk.Texture = null,
 65	
 66	        /// `notify::scale` handler id on `scale_surface`.
 67	        scale_notify_id: c_ulong = 0,
 68	
 69	        /// GdkSurface we connected; ref'd so a replacement cannot dangle the handler.
 70	        scale_surface: ?*gdk.Surface = null,
 71	
 72	        /// One-shot so we log the first real allocation, not every size-allocate.
 73	        scale_logged_size: bool = false,
